WEBVTT

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:14.260
And as for you,

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.120
I want you to disappear.

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:22.710
I see.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:25.500
Anisotropic being...

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:27.800
Tsukai Saraka.

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:05.180
Towanosakiwa'

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:10.710
Year | —

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:32.270
Ki: White

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:34.190
Wa: Other

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:36.280
Ki: Perception

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:37.440
Look

00:02:56.960 --> 00:03:05.220
Wa: Base

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:07.260
Ki:

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:09.060
Wa: A first

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:26.120
380,000 Years Later

00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:40.880
700 Million Years Later

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:53.440
Ki: What was that?

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:54.390
Sa: Gravity fluctuation.

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:55.400
Wa: An overdependence of mass.

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:56.440
To: A simple phenomenon.

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:57.310
No: It's continuing.

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:05.070
9.2 Billion Years Later

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:15.250
Wa: The mass preponderance is expanding.

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:16.670
Ki: A rare phenomenon. It's never occurred before.

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:18.290
Wa: Indeed.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:19.210
Ki: There is a special sense about it.

00:04:19.710 --> 00:04:27.090
Ki: The information in the entire cocoon is not sizable.

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:28.050
It can be read in an instant.

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:29.140
But even after you read it, something remains.

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:34.690
9.8 Billion Years Later

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:40.940
Ki: Anisotropic singularity.

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:41.480
To: Anisotropic singularity.

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:41.940
Wa: I want to touch the singularity.

00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:48.570
Ki: What will you do?

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:49.070
Wa: Go inside the cocoon.

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:49.620
No: What?

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:50.200
Sa: You're insane.

00:04:50.370 --> 00:05:04.340
To: The cocoon is a lower dimension.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:05:04.920
If you enter it, much information will be lost.

00:04:54.370 --> 00:05:05.420
Ki: Space will warp, and the cocoon will be destroyed.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:05:05.880
Sa: It's suicide.

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:06.470
No: What is your reason for doing this?

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:06.930
Wa: You understand, don't you?

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:17.310
Wa: I want to get closer.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:17.850
That's all.

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:18.310
Ki: Let's go.

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:18.900
Wa: I can't wait any longer!

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:25.280
4 Billion Years Ago

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:37.330
400 Million Years Ago

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:48.050
160 Million Years Ago

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:54.330
2.6 Million Years Ago

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:12.890
24 Years Ago

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:10.390
She laughed!

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:14.220
She's a girl, but she doesn't 
look any different from Satoru.

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:17.320
Well, she was just born!

00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:21.420
Did you think of a name?

00:06:23.470 --> 00:06:24.150
Yeah.

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:29.780
<b>Saraka</b>

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:29.230
Saraka?

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:32.280
You said it was a pretty name.

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:34.430
You liked them too, right?

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:35.830
The flowers on the tree in the yard.

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:39.410
The sarasouju tree... It is pretty,

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:42.080
but it's kind of an ephemeral name, isn't it?

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:44.830
Humans are ephemeral creatures.

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:49.240
We're just like a spring night's dream.

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:54.100
Nothing wrong with that, though.

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:56.010
Right, Saraka?

00:07:23.900 --> 00:07:25.660
Saraka!

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:28.630
Saraka!

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:32.740
Saraka!

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:48.030
Saraka!

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:14.340
I told you not to leave 
the house by yourself!

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:32.610
Saraka, listen.

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:36.110
Humans can die really easily.

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:43.120
That's we have to try our hardest 
to live, for as long as we're alive.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:45.960
Do you understand, Saraka?

00:08:49.160 --> 00:08:51.740
Well, you will someday.

00:09:03.350 --> 00:09:05.470
Okay, Dad. I'm off.

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:08.810
Dad?

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:12.820
You don't understand anything!

00:09:13.350 --> 00:09:17.570
There're guns everywhere in America!

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:22.330
What could a little girl like you do
if someone pointed a gun at you?

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:26.080
If you can't do what your parents tell you,

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:27.730
then just leave!

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:33.340
If I ever get into trouble, 
I'll just do what you told me!

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:35.670
What did you say?

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:37.810
Bye!

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:47.660
Come back soon.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:27.020
Yaha-kui zaShunina, 
I won't let you have your way!

00:10:27.380 --> 00:10:29.650
Oh? Why?

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:31.890
Because I am this universe's

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:34.190
biggest fan!

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:44.120
You set the initial conditions of the cocoon,

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:46.040
and then never touched it?

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:48.660
You're a naturalist?

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:53.340
It's a typical ideology in the anisotropic,

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:57.590
but it's not the right answer.

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:01.760
Saraka-san!

00:11:09.510 --> 00:11:11.810
When you descended into this cocoon,

00:11:11.810 --> 00:11:15.650
you gave up most of what made 
you an anisotropic being, right?

00:11:16.410 --> 00:11:19.790
I possess the full power of the anisotropic.

00:11:19.790 --> 00:11:20.980
You cannot fight me.

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:24.140
zaShunina.

00:11:26.260 --> 00:11:27.700
Tell me.

00:11:28.150 --> 00:11:30.210
What is the right answer?

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:36.370
The anisotropic beings created the 
cocoons in search of information,

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:38.710
and the universe created humanity.

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:41.580
Thus, humanity will be 
taken out of the cocoon,

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:43.850
and will encounter the anisotropic.

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:47.680
That is our final destination,

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:52.730
and the single, absolute answer for 
which humanity and the universe exist.

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:55.150
You're not telling me...

00:11:56.750 --> 00:11:59.110
You're going to take humanity 
to the anisotropic?

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:02.310
You already know, don't you, Shindo?

00:12:03.580 --> 00:12:07.870
Kado is a boundary object, 
but also a transforming device.

00:12:10.130 --> 00:12:11.590
I want to meet humanity.

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:15.860
Not in these cramped lower dimensions,

00:12:16.390 --> 00:12:18.080
but in the real world.

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:19.380
The anisotropic!

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:20.750
It's impossible!

00:12:20.750 --> 00:12:24.300
They can't endure the transformation 
from the universe to the anisotropic!

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:26.890
The amount of information 
is completely different!

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:31.390
If you do that, you'll break humanity!

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:33.980
It's true that the possibility is low,

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:37.000
but that is not a reason to stop it.

00:12:37.910 --> 00:12:38.990
I only need one.

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:41.750
Just one...

00:12:41.750 --> 00:12:46.600
A single successful transformation, 
and my objective will be achieved.

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:48.670
I have enough.

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:50.710
I can make copies.

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:52.870
I can just do it until I succeed.

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:55.870
You're wrong!

00:12:57.380 --> 00:13:00.440
The transformation to the anisotropic 
is for humanity's benefit, as well.

00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:04.030
Even if humanity were to continue 
to exist in this universe,

00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:07.090
their lifespan wouldn't 
even reach one billion years.

00:13:07.910 --> 00:13:10.660
If you truly desire humanity's 
continued existence,

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:13.600
the smart thing to do is 
to go to the anisotropic.

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:15.690
Thus, I will ask you, in light of this...

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:17.940
Where am I mistaken?

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:19.940
Mankind...

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:22.440
All of mankind...

00:13:22.850 --> 00:13:27.950
lives as best they can in 
the time they're given.

00:13:30.730 --> 00:13:32.840
That is our happiness.

00:13:34.030 --> 00:13:36.510
That is how humans live!

00:13:37.450 --> 00:13:39.210
This does not warrant discussion.

00:13:39.730 --> 00:13:42.770
zaShunina, I'll tell you, too.

00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:45.130
You're wrong.

00:13:46.950 --> 00:13:48.640
What is my mistake?

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:50.750
I can't tell you.

00:13:50.750 --> 00:13:51.560
Why?

00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:56.060
Because if I do, I'll no longer 
be able to correct it.

00:13:57.910 --> 00:14:00.280
It's to stop me, isn't it?

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:02.650
Lies make me sad.

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:03.940
zaShunina!

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:11.230
Shindo.

00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:16.540
I wanted you to come to the 
anisotropic of your own will.

00:14:17.020 --> 00:14:21.840
I wanted to reach the one right answer 
together with humanity and the anisotropic.

00:14:22.310 --> 00:14:23.450
But it seems...

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:26.340
that is impossible.

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:31.270
This is goodbye.

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:38.140
No, zaShunina!

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:44.020
Kado.

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:29.950
Sh-Shindo-san! Shindo-san!

00:15:31.340 --> 00:15:32.780
Open your eyes!

00:15:33.260 --> 00:15:35.030
Please, open your eyes!

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:37.080
Shindo-san, please!

00:15:39.110 --> 00:15:41.120
Shindo-san!

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:12.730
Shindo...

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:20.420
Please, make it in time!

00:16:32.470 --> 00:16:33.690
Shindo-san!

00:16:34.570 --> 00:16:35.840
Where are we?

00:16:36.290 --> 00:16:39.080
An isolated space I created.

00:16:39.080 --> 00:16:41.390
zaShunina can't find us here.

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:46.900
You really are an anisotropic 
being, aren't you?

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:48.720
I'm sorry.

00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:51.110
I know you probably can't trust me anymore,

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:55.410
but please, just trust me for right now!

00:17:01.740 --> 00:17:06.730
Why did you save me when it 
meant this would happen to you?

00:17:07.990 --> 00:17:10.610
You knew I was an anisotropic being!

00:17:11.420 --> 00:17:14.220
So why? Why?!

00:17:15.650 --> 00:17:18.390
There wasn't a reason.

00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:26.670
Sometimes we humans do strange things.

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:31.130
Shindo-san...

00:17:43.340 --> 00:17:47.170
I watched you for so long.

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:48.600
This universe.

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:50.580
Its life.

00:17:54.910 --> 00:17:56.090
Humanity.

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:04.740
Humanity bloomed for a single instant 
in the endless flow of the universe.

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:09.020
They live in that instant 
with all their might,

00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:14.050
and I fell in love with them for that.

00:18:16.870 --> 00:18:22.010
I love humanity.

00:18:44.070 --> 00:18:45.260
It's healing itself.

00:18:58.450 --> 00:18:59.900
Shindo-san!

00:19:01.630 --> 00:19:03.530
Are you okay, Shindo-kun?

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:06.030
A huge hole suddenly opened in Kado.

00:19:06.030 --> 00:19:08.810
And Tsukai-san went missing.

00:19:09.590 --> 00:19:11.390
And, um...

00:19:11.390 --> 00:19:14.880
Saraka-san was an anisotropic being.

00:19:15.550 --> 00:19:17.380
What are you talking about?

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:27.390
I've captured Tsukai Saraka within this.

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:30.210
She was causing damage.

00:19:30.210 --> 00:19:31.900
What's going on?

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:34.130
I'll explain everything.

00:19:34.130 --> 00:19:36.490
First, there's something I want you to see.

00:19:37.100 --> 00:19:38.150
Kado.

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:44.920
What is this?

00:19:45.710 --> 00:19:46.530
It can't be...

00:19:47.780 --> 00:19:50.080
The fourth anisotropic power.

00:19:50.570 --> 00:19:52.260
Nanomis-hein.

00:20:10.590 --> 00:20:11.830
I'm alive...

00:20:39.490 --> 00:20:40.930
Shindo-san!

00:20:43.590 --> 00:20:44.740
I'm so glad...

00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:48.300
Yeah.

00:20:49.420 --> 00:20:50.940
What's wrong?

00:20:50.940 --> 00:20:51.830
Nothing...

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:01.930
This is, um... just how it has to work!

00:21:04.900 --> 00:21:05.910
Thank you.

00:21:16.210 --> 00:21:19.650
To use the Nanomis-hein, 
you need inherent capability

00:21:16.850 --> 00:21:21.270
<b>Japanese-Anisotropic Joint Initiative Committee</b>

00:21:19.650 --> 00:21:21.460
as well as practice.

00:21:22.100 --> 00:21:26.450
We will find people like Dr. Shinawa 
Kanata and advance our research.

00:21:26.900 --> 00:21:31.250
That is the fastest way to use 
the Nanomis-hein worldwide.

00:21:32.720 --> 00:21:36.820
If you touch it, you can experience 
the touch sensation of the anisotropic.

00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:40.370
Anyone with the inherent
capability can understand

00:21:40.370 --> 00:21:43.050
its basic principles simply by doing that.

00:23:36.180 --> 00:23:38.900
Is there a way to stop zaShunina by force?

00:23:38.900 --> 00:23:43.150
Even if that weapon is completed, it may 
simply delay your death by a moment.

00:23:43.150 --> 00:23:45.770
You're too selfish, Shindo-san.

00:23:45.770 --> 00:23:49.640
You're an idiot, Shindo-san! A huge idiot!

00:23:48.550 --> 00:23:52.000
Wanoraru
